      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the `use_preference` boolean is an implementation detail that is relevant only to this particular implementation of the verifier (`FindFirstSupportedConfiguration()`), I\u0027m thinking that maybe we could keep the CodecManager interface as is and instead of changing its API and using a `std::placeholders::_3` here to route the boolean value via the CodecManager interface, we could just bind a function requiring 3 parameters (`FindFirstSupportedConfiguration(_, _, _)`) as a 2 parameter callback (`UnicastConfigurationVerifier(_, _)`) by simply providing this 3rd parameter value like this:\n```\n  auto new_conf \u003d CodecManager::GetInstance()-\u003eGetCodecConfig(\n          requirements,\n          std::bind(\u0026LeAudioDeviceGroup::FindFirstSupportedConfiguration, this,\n                    std::placeholders::_1, std::placeholders::_2, use_preferred));\n```\nThis makes the codec manager think that this is still a function taking 2 arguments, while in reality this binding wraps a function requiring 3 arguments and provides the missing 3rd boolean.\n\nWould that makes sense?",
